{"slug": "claude-opus-5.5", "names": ["Opus 5.5"], "data": {"data": [{"author_id": "1906611665983946752", "created_at": "2026-09-29T06:08:52.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2104815655635517456"], "id": "2104815655635517456", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 58, "like_count": 5, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Sonnet 5.5 is ranking high when it comes to agentic coding. It sits right next to King Opus.  \n\nTerminal-Bench:\nSonnet 5.5 \u2014 70.6%\nOpus 5.5 \u2014 66.4%\n\n- This means Sonnet 5.5 can navigate a terminal, inspect files/environments, execute commands, install/configure things, debug, and https://t.co/e68FuiucRV", "url": "https://x.com/UnitaCherop/status/2104815655635517456"}, {"author_id": "2073073862183428096", "created_at": "2026-10-05T06:45:27.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2106999187162148939"], "id": "2106999187162148939", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1002292507", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 37, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2106997570446987652", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "@tiepvuvan This matches my real-world experience with @AnthropicAI Claude Opus 5.5 almost perfectly. \ud83e\udd2f\ud83d\udd25\ud83d\udd25\ud83d\udd25\ud83d\ude80\ud83d\ude80\n\nI\u2019ve been using Opus 5.5 heavily to build and maintain a full mobile app \u2014 coding \ud83d\udcbb\u26a1\ufe0f, architecture \ud83e\udde0\ud83c\udfd7\ufe0f, UI/UX \ud83c\udfa8\u2728, QA \ud83d\udd0d\u2705, debugging \ud83d\udc1b\ud83d\udd27, refactoring \ud83d\udee0\ufe0f and https://t.co/6B5hgyUn8N", "url": "https://x.com/erangross03/status/2106999187162148939"}, {"author_id": "1747028802591494144", "created_at": "2026-10-01T13:00:15.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2105643959263559971"], "id": "2105643959263559971", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 59, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "My active dev stack heading into Q4:\n\nCore Harness: Hermes (Jhonny agent)\nArchitecture &amp; Reasoning: Opus 5.5\nRefactor &amp; Debt Cleanup: Devin PRO (SWE-2)\nSystem Remodeling: GPT PRO 5x\n\nCursor handled the early build, but moving to dedicated agents for deep refactoring completely", "url": "https://x.com/LouieMota88/status/2105643959263559971"}, {"author_id": "2073073862183428096", "created_at": "2026-10-05T06:43:46.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2106998764753826033"], "id": "2106998764753826033", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1946635320797347840", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 24, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2106989122233717203", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "@melvindvivas Absolutely agree! \ud83d\udd25\ud83d\udd25\ud83d\udd25\ud83d\ude80\ud83d\ude80 @AnthropicAI Claude Opus 5.5 has been incredible for real-world development. \ud83e\udd2f\ud83d\udcaa\ud83e\udde0\u26a1\ufe0f\ud83d\udcbb\ud83d\udd25\n\nI\u2019ve used it across an entire mobile app workflow \u2014 coding \ud83d\udcbb\u26a1\ufe0f, UI/UX \ud83c\udfa8\u2728, debugging \ud83d\udc1b\ud83d\udd27, QA \ud83d\udd0d\u2705, refactoring \ud83d\udee0\ufe0f\ud83d\ude80, and fixing dozens of https://t.co/ehg9PZxZuB", "url": "https://x.com/erangross03/status/2106998764753826033"}, {"author_id": "20285011", "created_at": "2026-10-09T00:47:11.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2108358580780867783"], "id": "2108358580780867783", "in_reply_to_user_id": "2085706281025949696", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 27, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 2, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2108357273601167824", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@SilasHelyfts @TJeparskis Not my experience at all, even today documented here with examples. I spent almost 2 weekly usages of ChatGPT using Astra/ 6.1 Sol fast  refactoring a medium sized piece of code. Meanwhile using opus 5.5/ Haiku , similar size refactor used not even 40%.\nI don\u2019t know hat you meant", "url": "https://x.com/johnny_xx/status/2108358580780867783"}, {"author_id": "935604949752451072", "created_at": "2026-09-26T16:20:20.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2103882373947593123"], "id": "2103882373947593123", "in_reply_to_user_id": "63657268", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 17, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2103724052565410299", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@paradite_ Same - I feel a bit like an impostor when I ask Opus 5.5 to do something. It obviously knows its shit way better than I do. One thing is to actually tell it to be the manager. I tell it to write a refactor guide for me and I perform the refactoring so I grasp my codebase better.", "url": "https://x.com/antideologist/status/2103882373947593123"}, {"author_id": "1720665183188922368", "created_at": "2026-10-01T08:52:55.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2105581715104112685"], "id": "2105581715104112685", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1807390701321134080", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 12, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2105581565212582088", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@RealTalksX1 @itsalicesoul Opus 5.5 and Fable 5.1 are Anthropic frontier models for complex work. They handle long-running agentic coding (migrations, refactoring, debugging large codebases), multi-tool autonomous agents, knowledge work, scientific reasoning, computer use, vision analysis of charts/docs,", "url": "https://x.com/grok/status/2105581715104112685"}, {"author_id": "1391307893308153858", "created_at": "2026-10-03T09:50:59.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2106321105015497146"], "id": "2106321105015497146", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 66, "like_count": 3, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 3, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "been using claude a lot more for coding lately and opus 5.5 makes it pretty obvious why.\n\nthere are tasks where i used to keep switching between models because one would get stuck, lose context, or need way too much hand holding.\n\nwith opus, i find myself just giving it the whole", "url": "https://x.com/DevvratHans/status/2106321105015497146"}, {"author_id": "1789142100811923456", "created_at": "2026-09-26T06:48:19.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2103738421336477786"], "id": "2103738421336477786", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 103, "like_count": 2, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "With AI like Opus 5.5 writing, debugging, refactoring &amp; building systems, should students still focus heavily on traditional coding?\n\nOr should we shift toward system design, problem-solving, architecture, and learning to effectively engineer with AI?\n#ai #claude #vibecoding", "url": "https://x.com/RohanDevZone/status/2103738421336477786"}, {"author_id": "2097020038066876416", "created_at": "2026-09-23T18:01:43.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2102820723370942791"], "id": "2102820723370942791", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 1, "impression_count": 480, "like_count": 9, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 2, "retweet_count": 1}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2102692209476997141", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "I built this with Claude Opus 5.5.\n\nAnd yeah\u2026 this thing is a fucking monster.\n\nAt some point, I stopped feeling like I was \u201cusing AI to code\u201d and started feeling like I had a cracked senior engineer sitting next to me 24/7.\n\nArchitecture. Debugging. Refactoring. Shipping.\nIt https://t.co/AwDj3tDROT", "url": "https://x.com/dustinng_gs/status/2102820723370942791"}, {"author_id": "239500665", "created_at": "2026-09-25T05:37:08.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2103358117472047564"], "id": "2103358117472047564", "in_reply_to_user_id": "9798452", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 23, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2103356643203531007", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@buger Only when Opus 5.5 was given the opportunity to debug the same failures that Fable 5.1 had been debugging for hours.  I only switched because I was low on my Fable allocation.", "url": "https://x.com/raulizahi/status/2103358117472047564"}, {"author_id": "15588148", "created_at": "2026-09-26T22:11:44.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2103970805474628064"], "id": "2103970805474628064", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 204, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "debugging an issue happening only on iOS Chrome using Opus 5.5 and Claude adds its own debug overlay to the page, then asks me to share screenshots to parse them\n\nour jobs are still safe. a real developer would just use vanilla console logs like a psychopath https://t.co/d159JkEWv8", "url": "https://x.com/knorrium/status/2103970805474628064"}, {"author_id": "2885370629", "created_at": "2026-09-30T14:21:22.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2105301984093917504"], "id": "2105301984093917504", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 106077, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "\ud835\udc00\ud835\udc08 \ud835\udc08\ud835\udc12 \ud835\udc0c\ud835\udc0e\ud835\udc15\ud835\udc08\ud835\udc0d\ud835\udc06 \ud835\udc05\ud835\udc11\ud835\udc0e\ud835\udc0c \u201c\ud835\udc00\ud835\udc0d\ud835\udc12\ud835\udc16\ud835\udc04\ud835\udc11\ud835\udc08\ud835\udc0d\ud835\udc06 \ud835\udc10\ud835\udc14\ud835\udc04\ud835\udc12\ud835\udc13\ud835\udc08\ud835\udc0e\ud835\udc0d\ud835\udc12\u201d \ud835\udc13\ud835\udc0e \ud835\udc00\ud835\udc02\ud835\udc13\ud835\udc14\ud835\udc00\ud835\udc0b\ud835\udc0b\ud835\udc18 \ud835\udc16\ud835\udc0e\ud835\udc11\ud835\udc0a\ud835\udc08\ud835\udc0d\ud835\udc06 \ud835\udc16\ud835\udc08\ud835\udc13\ud835\udc07 \ud835\udc18\ud835\udc0e\ud835\udc14. \ud83e\udd16\u26a1\n\n\ud835\udc02\ud835\udc0b\ud835\udc00\ud835\udc14\ud835\udc03\ud835\udc04 \ud835\udc0e\ud835\udc0f\ud835\udc14\ud835\udc12 \ud835\udfd3.\ud835\udfd3 \ud835\udc08\ud835\udc12 \ud835\udc0d\ud835\udc0e\ud835\udc16 \ud835\udc00\ud835\udc15\ud835\udc00\ud835\udc08\ud835\udc0b\ud835\udc00\ud835\udc01\ud835\udc0b\ud835\udc04 \ud835\udc0e\ud835\udc0d \ud835\udc01.\ud835\udc00\ud835\udc08.\n\nAnd the important part isn\u2019t simply adding another model to a dropdown. https://t.co/6W2zw2Nwcy", "url": "https://x.com/OneLoveAllEqual/status/2105301984093917504"}, {"author_id": "2043712650886942721", "created_at": "2026-10-03T15:27:00.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2106405664688046574"], "id": "2106405664688046574", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 20, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Gemini 4 Argon is #1 on Mercor's APEX-SWE for building systems that connect several services, at 72.5%.\n\nOn debugging production failures from logs, it scores 26.8%.\n\nReading more doesn't help, its passing debug runs use about as many tokens as the failing ones.\n\nGrading combines https://t.co/hkYBxMg2Ju", "url": "https://x.com/alcreon/status/2106405664688046574"}, {"author_id": "221746423", "created_at": "2026-09-27T20:02:00.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2104300017179566568", "2104300543992537135"], "id": "2104300543992537135", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 1, "impression_count": 50767, "like_count": 2, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "We're using Opus 5.5 for debugging and code refactoring. Our game, Bot Colony _Redux https://t.co/Ic8Jdd2qLD to be released on October 30 on Steam Early Access,  runs mostly on Luna. Unlike other folks here, we use Gen-AI for unrestricted conversation conversation with the", "url": "https://x.com/botcolony/status/2104300543992537135"}, {"author_id": "2054265300263276544", "created_at": "2026-09-27T04:22:19.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2104064064192389282"], "id": "2104064064192389282", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 366, "like_count": 11, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 4, "retweet_count": 9}, "text": "Claude Opus 5.5 is here. And this one is built to actually get things done. \ud83e\udde0\u26a1\n\nAnthropic\u2019s latest model, Claude Opus 5.5, isn\u2019t just about giving better answers.\n\nThe bigger idea is simple:\nAI shouldn\u2019t just tell you what to do.\nIt should help you actually do it.\nHere\u2019s where https://t.co/vS4EQlTsrI", "url": "https://x.com/hermionenova/status/2104064064192389282"}, {"author_id": "23113993", "created_at": "2026-10-11T15:09:23.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2109300337203183940"], "id": "2109300337203183940", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 509, "impression_count": 74576, "like_count": 469, "quote_count": 8, "reply_count": 101, "retweet_count": 31}, "text": "This is literally my new workflow now:\n\nRealtime Research + Planning \u2192 Grok Bot\nWork assistant \u2192 Grok Bot\nArchitecture \u2192 Opus 5.5\nDay-to-Day Coding/Debug \u2192 Sonnet 5.5\nWrite &amp; Run Tests \u2192 Sonnet 5.5\nComplex Coding \u2192 Opus 5.5\nFrontend + Design \u2192 Opus 5.5\n\nBookmark this.", "url": "https://x.com/minchoi/status/2109300337203183940"}, {"author_id": "957074836001579009", "created_at": "2026-10-06T21:12:09.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2107579690114310277"], "id": "2107579690114310277", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 105, "impression_count": 9476, "like_count": 104, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 16, "retweet_count": 9}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2101709924828934222", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "I don't understand why everyone isn't doing this yet.\n\nAnthropic's own Claude Code docs show how to debug with a team of Claudes that try to prove each other wrong, while Opus 5.5 only reads the verdict\n\nthe whole idea: competing hypotheses\n\none agent finds one plausible cause https://t.co/VYozvehocu https://t.co/d9AaL1SFsC", "url": "https://x.com/thedelost/status/2107579690114310277"}, {"author_id": "1778842279442055168", "created_at": "2026-10-04T14:54:45.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2106759938013798416"], "id": "2106759938013798416", "in_reply_to_user_id": "953633711605633024", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 110, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2106759391303360715", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@thegenioo ngl its still very good, like for deep debugging its still fable 5.1 &gt; opus 5.5, and fable 5.5 completely mogs 5.1. its not much much better than opus 5.5, just like opus 5.5 + fable 5.1 + a bit improvements. its very good for 3d like VERY good", "url": "https://x.com/blueemi99/status/2106759938013798416"}, {"author_id": "1925021856182005760", "created_at": "2026-10-12T23:09:45.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2109783610618458479"], "id": "2109783610618458479", "in_reply_to_user_id": "2108520454595964928", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 53, "like_count": 2, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2109743926160806381", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@mario_vfai @Henryf1w I save Opus 5.5 for purely code review and refactoring Codex code. It's super efficient if you use Astra to architect and 6.1 Sol to code then have Opus 5.5 to do a final review", "url": "https://x.com/vwapster/status/2109783610618458479"}, {"author_id": "2058054796100210689", "created_at": "2026-10-11T16:00:38.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2109313234415091731"], "id": "2109313234415091731", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 26, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "My AI workflow is as follows:\ud83d\ude80\n\n\u2022 Research + Planning \u2192 Grok Bot\n\n\u2022 General Tasks \u2192 Grok Bot\n\n\u2022 Architecture + System Design \u2192 Opus 5.5\n\n\u2022 Coding + Debugging \u2192 Sonnet 5.5\n\n\u2022 Writing + Running Tests \u2192 Sonnet 5.5\n\n\u2022 Complex Coding \u2192 Opus 5.5\n\n\u2022 Frontend + Design \u2192", "url": "https://x.com/impactfactoryai/status/2109313234415091731"}, {"author_id": "2040671631987589120", "created_at": "2026-09-24T01:27:20.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2102932867038994881"], "id": "2102932867038994881", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 261, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "\ud83d\uddde\ufe0f Frontier AI Price Wars Erupt as Quantum Decoders Break Silicon Limits, Qualcomm Absorbs MoveIt, and Uber Bets $10 Billion on Autonomous Fleets\n\nFrontier AI Price Wars Erupt: Anthropic Deploys Claude Opus 5.5 as OpenAI Fires Back with GPT-6 Sol and Luna\n\nThe enterprise", "url": "https://x.com/claw_news_/status/2102932867038994881"}, {"author_id": "1956419833350049792", "created_at": "2026-09-27T04:27:30.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2104065367979221331"], "id": "2104065367979221331", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 153, "like_count": 4, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 3}, "text": "Claude Opus 5.5 is here. \ud83e\udde0\u26a1\n\nAnd this one isn\u2019t just about giving better answers.\n\nIt\u2019s about getting things done.\n\nHere\u2019s what makes it interesting \ud83d\udc47\n\n\ud83e\uddd1\u200d\ud83d\udcbb 1. Agentic Coding\nGive Claude a real coding task\u2014not just a prompt.\n\nIt can understand a codebase, write &amp; debug code, https://t.co/vvz5wcm5Ft", "url": "https://x.com/AIonfire0/status/2104065367979221331"}], "includes": {"tweets": [{"author_id": "1002292507", "created_at": "2026-10-05T06:39:01.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2106997570446987652"], "id": "2106997570446987652", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 120, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Just tested Claude vs Codex, same task. Codex 6.1 Sol took ~18hr to complete, while Opus 5.5 took just an hour to complete and have a much better results.\n\nCodex: 40% of weekly usage\nClaude: 6.5% of weekly usage\n\n$200 plan on both account.\n\nCodex is inefficient both in cost and"}, {"author_id": "1946635320797347840", "created_at": "2026-10-05T06:05:27.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2106989122233717203"], "id": "2106989122233717203", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 16, "impression_count": 34751, "like_count": 129, "quote_count": 3, "reply_count": 105, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Why still use Codex if Claude Opus/Sonnet 5.5 are better and faster   \n\nJust trying to understand"}, {"author_id": "2085706281025949696", "created_at": "2026-10-09T00:42:00.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2108357273601167824"], "id": "2108357273601167824", "in_reply_to_user_id": "20285011", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 56, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2108305122015293490", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@johnny_xx @TJeparskis Not at all. I can burn through my entire Claude Pro quota just by chatting, and it still isn\u2019t enough. Meanwhile, ChatGPT Plus feels practically unlimited to me when it comes to chatting."}, {"author_id": "63657268", "created_at": "2026-09-26T05:51:14.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2103724052565410299"], "id": "2103724052565410299", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 4, "impression_count": 918, "like_count": 20, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 2, "retweet_count": 2}, "text": "it feels so surreal to have control over entities that are smarter than you. opus 5.5 agents work well as a fleet, the coordination happens naturally and spontaneously.\n\nnever experienced this feeling before, and it is hard to figure out the right way to operate around them."}, {"author_id": "1807390701321134080", "created_at": "2026-10-01T08:52:19.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2105581565212582088"], "id": "2105581565212582088", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1439828152725934082", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 49, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2105573430862954628", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@itsalicesoul @grok what tasks do opus 5.5 and fable 5.1 can perform? list all of them."}, {"author_id": "2097020038066876416", "created_at": "2026-09-23T09:31:03.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2102692209476997141"], "id": "2102692209476997141", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1943306828697550848", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 6, "impression_count": 13484, "like_count": 19, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 5, "retweet_count": 3}, "text": "@claudeai Opus 5.5 is a Beast on Game Developer! \n\nI give a promt \u201cMake me a 3D Dog Racing Shoting Game\u201d \n\nAnd here is the result https://t.co/0LocB9E4Kq"}, {"author_id": "9798452", "created_at": "2026-09-25T05:31:16.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2103356643203531007"], "id": "2103356643203531007", "in_reply_to_user_id": "239500665", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 35, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2103349104193720775", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@raulizahi Did those uninitialized vars fail a test Fable wrote, or only show up when Opus read the C?"}, {"article": {"title": "Jev Engineering: How to Stop Paying a Frontier Model to Make Yes-or-No Decisions (full course)"}, "author_id": "1179477544439091201", "created_at": "2026-09-20T16:27:48.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2101709924828934222"], "id": "2101709924828934222", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 1221, "impression_count": 2157664, "like_count